                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237176299",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198035768850",
                            "num_reviews": 119,
                            "playtime_forever": 194,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 178,
                            "last_played": 1791473997
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel like there is a decent little puzzle game in here, but it is held back by two incredibly irritating factors; For one, the enemy movement is completely randomized. That means it is a crapshoot on if you're able to go past enemies to collect the keys without any issue or if they somehow perfectly zero in on you to reset whatever progress you've made. And two, there is a hidden time limit where if you take too long to complete a level you are pursued and killed by a massive ghost. It feels like the time is the exact same per level regardless of its length or difficulty, and running out of time is incredibly frustrating when you're waiting for the randomly moving enemies to get out of the way of the level's exit.\n\nWith a bit more polish and a few tweaks here and there, this game has the potential to be decent. As the game is though, it is far more annoying than fun. Not recommended.",
